WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.777 --> 00:00:17.805
"So wasn't the one who dumped the frogs back in the pool," Maggie said.

2
00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:21.107
"But that doesn't mean she didn't do the other stuff.

3
00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:24.389
Like put the frogs in the pool the first time.

4
00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:27.130
Or put ants on Daisy's towel."

5
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.772
"True," Henry agreed.

6
00:00:30.668 --> 00:00:32.869
"But why would she do that to Daisy?

7
00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:36.970
Did Daisy say something about her looking young too?"

8
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.291
"I don't think so," Cole said.

9
00:00:40.311 --> 00:00:45.372
"Then Lauren probably didn't do the ant prank either," Henry said.

10
00:00:45.392 --> 00:00:48.213
"Let's talk about our other suspects."

11
00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:50.914
"You mean Kyle and Tommy?"

12
00:00:51.294 --> 00:00:52.094
Maggie asked.

13
00:00:52.114 --> 00:00:55.915
"I still don't think Tommy did it," Cole said.

14
00:00:55.935 --> 00:00:57.595
"He's my friend."

15
00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:00.669
"Okay," Henry said.

16
00:01:00.689 --> 00:01:03.350
"But he does have a good motive.

17
00:01:04.451 --> 00:01:08.514
If you get kicked out of tryouts, he has a better chance of making the team."

18
00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:13.697
"It didn't seem like he really cares about making the team," Maggie said.

19
00:01:13.717 --> 00:01:18.140
"Don't forget that his brother is a star," Henry said.

20
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.963
"What if Tommy cares more about the team than he's showing?

21
00:01:24.024 --> 00:01:27.626
And it would be easy for him to get the frogs from his parents' pet store."

22
00:01:28.647 --> 00:01:29.808
Maggie's eyes lit up.

23
00:01:30.712 --> 00:01:33.554
"Plus Tommy was the one who gave Daisy that towel.

24
00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:38.216
He might have poured grape drink on it, and then dragged it through an anthill."

25
00:01:38.236 --> 00:01:42.679
"That doesn't sound like something Tommy would do," Cole said.

26
00:01:42.699 --> 00:01:44.820
"Aren't there any other suspects?"

27
00:01:46.101 --> 00:01:47.482
"Sure," Henry said.

28
00:01:47.502 --> 00:01:52.044
"The other two people with good motives are Kyle and Daisy."

29
00:01:52.065 --> 00:01:54.786
"Daisy?" Maggie said.

30
00:01:54.806 --> 00:01:57.828
"But she's the one who got attacked by ants!"

31
00:01:59.356 --> 00:02:02.058
"She could have set that up herself," Henry said.

32
00:02:02.078 --> 00:02:06.300
"That way nobody would suspect her of the frog prank."

33
00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.062
"Maybe." Cole looked unsure.

34
00:02:10.082 --> 00:02:12.543
"It doesn't seem very likely though.

35
00:02:13.564 --> 00:02:14.524
She almost got bitten.

36
00:02:15.285 --> 00:02:16.886
And ant bites really hurt."

37
00:02:17.966 --> 00:02:19.927
Just then Lauren wandered past.

38
00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:23.089
"Hey," she said, pointing at Cole.

39
00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:26.771
"Aren't you supposed to be the frog expert around here?"

40
00:02:28.212 --> 00:02:28.712
He nodded.

41
00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.140
"Then help catch those frogs!"

42
00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:35.982
"Okay." Cole waved to his friends and swam away.

43
00:02:36.002 --> 00:02:41.063
"I guess Lauren knows that Cole likes frogs," Maggie said to Henry.

44
00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:43.924
"Are you sure she's not the culprit?"

45
00:02:45.344 --> 00:02:46.825
Maggie's voice was pretty loud.

46
00:02:47.845 --> 00:02:53.147
Henry didn't want everyone to hear them talking, so he led her over to the playground.

47
00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.987
The two of them sat down on the swings.

48
00:02:57.208 --> 00:02:59.524
"I'm pretty sure," Henry told Maggie.

49
00:02:59.544 --> 00:03:03.645
"Lauren had no reason to make those ants swarm Daisy."

50
00:03:03.666 --> 00:03:07.527
"What if the ant prank was just a coincidence?"

51
00:03:07.947 --> 00:03:08.707
Maggie asked.

52
00:03:08.727 --> 00:03:15.349
"Maybe Tiny spilled grape juice on his towel, and then Tommy dragged it through an anthill without noticing."

53
00:03:15.369 --> 00:03:18.450
"It's possible," Henry said.

54
00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.611
"But I'm still pretty sure about Lauren.

55
00:03:22.711 --> 00:03:26.612
She couldn't have dumped the frog buckets while she was jogging behind the pool building."

56
00:03:28.116 --> 00:03:29.337
"I guess that's true."

57
00:03:30.097 --> 00:03:30.738
Maggie said.

58
00:03:30.758 --> 00:03:34.160
"It had to be one of the joggers who finished first.

59
00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:37.382
Who's the fastest runner out of our suspects?"

60
00:03:38.562 --> 00:03:40.803
"Probably Kyle," Henry said.

61
00:03:40.824 --> 00:03:43.605
"He was on the track team at school."

62
00:03:43.625 --> 00:03:48.268
"And we saw him with a grape sports drink," Maggie said.

63
00:03:48.288 --> 00:03:52.610
"Plus we know he really wants the spot on the swim team.

64
00:03:53.651 --> 00:03:55.072
He has to be the culprit!"

65
00:03:56.148 --> 00:03:59.970
"We have to be able to prove it's Kyle," Henry reminded her.

66
00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:03.451
"Let's go talk to him and see what we can find out."

67
00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:09.233
They found Kyle chasing a frog in the pool.

68
00:04:12.935 --> 00:04:14.476
Kyle," Henry greeted him.

69
00:04:14.496 --> 00:04:18.297
"Can you believe those frogs got in the water again?"

70
00:04:18.317 --> 00:04:21.678
"I can't believe it!"

71
00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:22.679
Kyle said.

72
00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:25.200
"Your friend Cole is a troublemaker.

73
00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.482
I hope the coach kicks him out this time!"

74
00:04:29.463 --> 00:04:30.504
Maggie scowled.

75
00:04:30.524 --> 00:04:32.545
"Cole didn't do it!"

76
00:04:32.565 --> 00:04:35.328
"That's not what everybody else says."

77
00:04:36.268 --> 00:04:38.310
Kyle grinned and puffed out his chest.

78
00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:43.134
"Once Cole's gone, that spot on the team will be all mine!"

79
00:04:44.595 --> 00:04:46.176
Henry traded a look with Maggie.

80
00:04:47.017 --> 00:04:48.879
He could tell they were thinking the same thing.

81
00:04:49.859 --> 00:04:51.140
Kyle sounded guilty!

82
00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.763
"You're a chicken, Kyle!"

83
00:04:54.103 --> 00:04:55.244
Maggie said angrily.

84
00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:57.921
"You're afraid Cole will beat you."

85
00:04:57.941 --> 00:05:00.761
"No way," Kyle said.

86
00:05:00.781 --> 00:05:02.842
"I'm not afraid of anybody!

87
00:05:03.642 --> 00:05:06.063
Having Cole out of the way just makes it easier.

88
00:05:07.543 --> 00:05:11.364
Maybe he should take some of these frogs home with him so they can teach him how to

89
00:05:11.465 --> 00:05:17.826
swim." Kyle laughed loudly, as if that was the funniest thing anyone had ever said.

90
00:05:18.647 --> 00:05:19.707
But Henry frowned.

91
00:05:20.847 --> 00:05:21.648
"What do you mean?"

92
00:05:22.028 --> 00:05:23.088
he asked Kyle.

93
00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:26.269
"Cole already has a bunch of pet frogs."

94
00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.911
"Really?" Kyle looked surprised.

95
00:05:29.931 --> 00:05:33.332
"So that's why John called Cole 'frog boy.'"

96
00:05:34.352 --> 00:05:36.613
Henry was still watching Kyle closely.

97
00:05:36.633 --> 00:05:39.855
"You didn't know that Cole has frogs?"

98
00:05:40.975 --> 00:05:41.735
Kyle shrugged.

99
00:05:41.755 --> 00:05:45.957
"I don't pay much attention to fifth-grade nerds," he said.

100
00:05:45.977 --> 00:05:50.139
"Speaking of which, why am I standing here talking to you?"

101
00:05:51.059 --> 00:05:52.780
He smirked and then swam away.

102
00:05:53.916 --> 00:05:55.900
"What a jerk," Maggie muttered.

103
00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:59.386
"He might be a jerk," Henry said.

104
00:05:59.406 --> 00:06:02.752
"But he's definitely not our culprit."
